      "Language": "spa",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "BACKGROUND",
          "Label": "BACKGROUND",
          "content": "The association of prevalence of obesity and asthma has increased significantly, this phenomenon seems multifactorial. Obesity is considered a risk factor for asthma. It has been reported positive association between obesity and allergic asthma. In Mexico there is no conclusive data about this issue."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "METHODS",
          "content": "The study was conducted in patients from 4 to 14 years of age, with allergic asthma. A history and physical examination and BMI estimation were performed, as well as the classification of asthma severity."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "We included 244 patients diagnosed with childhood allergic asthma, Fifty two patients (21.31%, OR 3.6) showed some degree of obesity (above the 85 percentile), 15.1% were male and 6% were female. Morbid obesity was found in 40 patients (16.3%)."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "content": "Our study found an increased prevalence of obesity in children with asthma, with a predominance in male gender, and showed a high association between the severity of asthma and increased BMI."
        }
      ]},
